HYPOTHESIS UNDER TEST
---------------------
H_B: "The six-event limit is imposed by FR32's specification, not by data
availability — i.e. the corpus contains materially more independently-datable
Indian systemic-stress episodes with full RMT+Hamilton coverage than the six
FR32 names."

H_0 (the complement): the limit is substantially data-bound — either the pillar
span is too short to contain materially more episodes, or additional episodes
lack the RMT+Hamilton coverage needed to score them.

PRE-REGISTERED DECISION RULE
----------------------------
H_B is ACCEPTED iff ALL THREE of the following hold:

  (B1) COUNT. >= 4 candidate episodes exist inside the *pillar-covered* span
       that are (i) not among FR32's six, (ii) datable from a public record
       exogenous to any SERAPH output, and (iii) not a re-slicing of an FR32
       episode. Operational non-overlap test, fixed now: a candidate's onset
       must be >= 60 trading days from every FR32 onset AND from every other
       accepted candidate onset. 60 = CRISIS_WINDOW_DAYS(30) + LEAD_WINDOW
       upper(15), rounded up, so that no two accepted events share a crisis
       window or a lead window.

  (B2) COVERAGE. For each accepted candidate, >= 95% of the trading days in
       [onset - 15, onset + 30] have non-null RMT output AND non-null Hamilton
       output in the DB. A candidate below 95% is counted as data-blocked, not
       as evidence for H_B.

  (B3) SPEC-BOUND, NOT DATA-BOUND. The number "6" must be traceable to a
       specification artefact (FR32 text, the EpochId Literal, EPOCH_BREAKS,
       preregistration.EPOCHS, D5 fold counts) and NOT to a data-availability
       boundary. Concretely: if the pillar span start (2005) is itself forced by
       an irreducible data limit AND >= 2 of the FR32-excluded candidates fall
       before that start, then the limit is at least partly data-bound and (B3)
       fails for those candidates.

H_B is REJECTED if (B1) fails. H_B is PARTIALLY SUPPORTED (reported as such, not
as acceptance) if (B1) and (B3) hold but (B2) fails for enough candidates to
bring the covered count below 4.

PRE-REGISTERED SOURCE RULE FOR CANDIDATE DATING
-----------------------------------------------
A candidate onset date is admissible ONLY if it is fixed by an event exogenous to
Indian equity prices and to every SERAPH signal:
  - a dated policy/administrative action (RBI/SEBI/Govt notification, PBoC fix,
    Fed statement, election result declaration), OR
  - a dated foreign/global event with an unambiguous calendar date.
INADMISSIBLE, declared now: any date chosen because the Indian market fell that
day, any date chosen by inspecting rmt_output / hamilton_output / csrs /
hawkes_output, any date chosen to maximise a drawdown or an AUC. Where the
exogenous date is a non-trading day in India, the onset is moved forward to the
next NSE trading day and that adjustment is recorded. The candidate list is
fixed BEFORE coverage is measured; coverage can only remove candidates, never
add them.

PRE-REGISTERED POWER PROTOCOL
-----------------------------
Extend scripts/early_warning_power.py's measured design (circular-shift
relocation null + AAFT surrogate null, AR(1) stationary-init background at the
real rv_t_yz lag-1 autocorrelation) to N in {6, 10, 15, 20} synthetic onsets on
the SAME real trading-day grid, with the real minimum onset spacing respected.
Reported per N: mean T3 AUC by injected effect delta in {0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0},
the delta=0 type-I error (the negative control — if it is not near 0.05 the row
is void and will be labelled void), and the MDE = smallest tested delta reaching
>= 80% power. Power is computed against the null, not against nominal 0.5.
Pass/fail is not applicable here; this arm is descriptive.

WHAT WOULD FALSIFY MY OWN CONCLUSION
------------------------------------
If the delta=0 negative control at N=10/15/20 does not land near 0.05, the
power-gain numbers are void and I must say so rather than reporting a curve.
If candidate coverage is high but the onsets cluster (fail the 60-day test),
the apparent gain in N is spurious dependence and I must report the effective,
not nominal, event count.

